          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Contributions to Geography and Science</strong><br>\nHumboldt's work laid the foundations for the field of biogeography. His \"Essay on the Geography of Plants,\" published in 1807, was a pioneering work that charted the distribution of organic life based on environmental conditions.</p>\n\n<p><strong>\"Kosmos\" and Views on the Universe</strong><br>\nHumboldt's later years were devoted to writing \"Kosmos,\" a multi-volume work attempting to unify the various branches of scientific knowledge under the idea of nature as an interconnected whole.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Exploration in Russia</strong><br>\nIn 1829, Humboldt led an expedition to Russia and Central Asia, sponsored by the Russian government. He made significant findings regarding the Earth's magnetic field and further contributions to the fields of climatology and oceanography.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
