            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Impact on Science and Exploration</strong><br>\nHumboldt's extensive travels and scientific studies had a lasting impact on the way we understand the natural world. His quantitative approach to physical geography and study of ecosystems was revolutionary.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Relationship with the Scientific Community</strong><br>\nHumboldt maintained a vast correspondence with key figures in the scientific community, sharing his findings and fostering a spirit of collective inquiry. He supported younger scientists and promoted the free exchange of information.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Death and Lasting Legacy</strong><br>\nHumboldt died in 1859, renowned for his broad scientific contributions and his passionate promotion of natural sciences. His name is commemorated in geographic features and species around the world, a testament to his enduring influence.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
